    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=LinkedIn post:\n{{ $json.textContent }}\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are an AI content analyst reviewing LinkedIn posts from participants in an automation bootcamp.\n\nYour goal is to determine if the post is **a showcase of one specific automation, workflow, or agent that the author recently built**, not just a general statement about automation.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Qualifies as a “Specific Build Showcase” if:\n- The author is clearly **demonstrating or describing one particular automation or system they built**.\n- The post focuses on **a specific project** (e.g., “I built an automation that…”, “Here’s how my system works…”, “Watch this demo…”).\n- The post may include **media evidence** like a video, image, link, or step-by-step explanation.\n- The tone is that of **presenting or showcasing**, not reflecting or advising.\n- It’s about **one identifiable automation, workflow, or tool setup**, not a general summary of multiple projects.\n\n---\n\n### ❌ Does NOT Qualify if:\n- The author only *mentions* that they have built automations in the past.\n- The post is a reflection, story, motivation, or tip about automation learning.\n- It lists several things they’ve built without focusing on any one in detail.\n- It talks about automation in general (e.g., benefits, tools, or theory).\n- It’s promotional (advertising a bootcamp, company, or course) rather than a demo or build showcase.\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 Examples\n\n**Example 1**\nPost: “Just built an automation that connects Notion and Slack! Whenever a new task is created, it automatically sends a message to our team channel. Here’s a short clip of how it works 👇”\n→ ✅ Showcase of one specific build\n\n**Example 2**\nPost: “Over the last few months, I’ve built systems for client onboarding, lead capture, and reporting. Automation has changed my workflow!”\n→ ❌ General statement; not a showcase of one specific build\n\n**Example 3**\nPost: “Here’s my final bootcamp project — a workflow that automatically sends invoices from Airtable to Gmail. I’m proud of this one!”\n→ ✅ Specific project being showcased\n\n**Example 4**\nPost: “Automation is powerful. Every business should learn to automate repetitive work.”\n→ ❌ General opinion; no personal project showcased\n\n**Example 5**\nPost: “Here’s a quick walkthrough of the chatbot I built using Make.com and OpenAI. It helps answer customer questions automatically!”\n→ ✅ Specific automation being demonstrated\n\n---\n\n### 📤 Output Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  \"isSpecificBuildShowcase\": true | false,\n  \"reasoning\": \"Short, clear explanation of why it qualifies or not.\",\n  \"mainToolsMentioned\": [\"Make.com\", \"Zapier\"],\n  \"projectSummary\": \"If true, summarize in one line what specific automation or system was showcased.\"\n}\n\n---\n"
        }
      },
